{
  "what": "A census of every PURCHASABLE row on the live Vault Store shelf in production (is_active AND gem_cost > 0), with the fields that decide whether the product can actually deliver it: slug, category, gem_cost, and the fulfillment metadata. No member data, no redemptions, no prices beyond the shelf price.",
  "why": "Backlog LIVE-013. The store charged Gems for five borders, five flairs and four titles whose only reader in the whole product was a text chip in the buyer's own Vault, and for five more SKUs whose metadata was `{}`, which routed them to an operator queue that did not exist. Three real paid redemptions (950 Gems, one member, 2026-06-27) had already happened. `scripts/check-cosmetic-renders.mjs` measures this shelf against the render registry (lib/store/cosmetics.ts), so a SKU that can be bought and cannot be shown fails CI instead of quietly taking someone's currency.",
  "howToRecapture": "Run the SQL in `recaptureQuery` against production (READ-ONLY) and rewrite `shelf` from the result, then set `capturedAt`. Re-capture after any /admin/store edit that adds, activates, reprices or re-metadatas a SKU. The guard reads the registry live, so it does NOT need a re-capture when the registry changes.",
  "scope": "store_items only. The three cosmetic COLUMNS on profiles (profile_border / profile_flair / custom_title) are the delivery target and are read live by the registry; profile_theme is a separate system (lib/theme/profile-skins.ts, rendered by the Spotlight shell) and is not sold in the store, so it is out of scope here.",
  "capturedAt": "2026-08-18",
  "project": "Frequency Community (azsqfeonabsbmemvddqd)",
  "recaptureQuery": "select slug, category::text as category, gem_cost, is_active, metadata from store_items where is_active and gem_cost > 0 order by category, slug;",
